ared is 36 10 squared is 10 times 10  100 if we subtract 36 from both sides of  the equation we get x squared equals 64  and if you take the square root of both  sides you're getting x equals 8 and  that's the missing side okay so for  number 73 now it says find the area of  the trapezoid and remember a trapezoid  is when you have a quadrilateral with  exactly one pair of opposite sides  parallel but these sides are not  parallel remember the formula for area  of a trapezoid it's 1/2 times the height  times the sum of the two bases now the  two bases are the two parallel signs in  this case is going to be 8 and 10 and  then the height is the perpendicular  distance between those two parallel  sides in this case it's 4 so if we  simplify you can see we're getting 18  times 4 times 1/2 1/2 times 4 is 2 2  times 18 is 36 so this is going to be 36  centimeters squared so areas units  squared so you might want to write down  that area of a trapezoid formula 474  we're working with a circle and we want  to find the circumference which is the  distance around the circle and then the  area that's the course the inside of the  circle so a couple more formulas you  want to remember circumference is 2 pi R  so 2 times 3.14 which is pi times the  radius and the area is equal to PI R  squared so the radius squared so for  here the circumference 2 times the  radius would be 2 times 4 which is 8  times pi so that's going to be 8 pi  meters  but the area is pi times 4 squared 4  squared is 4 times 4 which is 16 so we  get 16 pi meters squared 475 now it says  find the mean median and mode we're kind  of talking about statistics a little bit  here me means the average median means  the middle and mode means the one that  occurs the most but when you do this you  want to write the numbers in order from  Lois  to highest so I just rearranged it from  low to high so when we think about the  mean the mean is like the average so we  have to add all these up and divide by  how many we have so we have 5 plus 6  which is 11 plus 7 which is 18 plus 7 is  25 plus 10 is 35 divided by 5 numbers so  you can see that the mean is 7 okay now  for the median that's the middle number  so we have 5 + 10 6 + 7 7 is the one in  the middle so that's going to be our  median if there's two numbers that are  in the middle then what you would do is  you would add them together and divide  by 2 so it's like an average of the two  middle numbers and the mode is the one  that occurs the most so you can see  there's two 7s so the mode is 7 so it  looks like all of our answers came out  to 7 now if there was two 7s and two  sixes then the mode would be 6 and 7 say  for example if all the numbers were  listed just once then there would be no  mode ok and for number 76 it says what  is the probability of drawing a red  marble well when we talk about  probability we're talking about the  number of successful outcomes or I'll  just write the number of successes  divided by the total possible outcome so  if we reach into this hat blindfolded  right we say what's the problem we pick  a red marble well there's 3 red marbles  so 3 chances of picking a red marble a  success / 5 marbles total so our  probability is equal to 3/5 so you got  this if you want to see my algebra one  giant review check out the video right  there and I'll see you over in that  video
 

